From 6a758dbb9af1377df87144eec846bbe532e85a18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: derpsn <callmederpsn@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:42:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] Linux 0.8.0: only the native plug-in; the Access files
 are unpacked (msiextract or Wine), not installed

- install.sh: no Wine prefix install, no classic plug-in / yabridge step; the Access .msi is unpacked with msiextract
  (msitools) or, without it, Wine's administrative extraction into a throw-away prefix; Virus Control.dll,
  firmware.bin, manuals -> ~/.local/share/tirevive/access, factory patch libraries -> ~/Documents (missing files
  only); an Access installation of TI Revive 0.7 in the Wine prefix is reused; the classic plug-in (prefix +
  yabridge copy) and test bundles are removed
- tarball without wine/ (classic plug-in, MSI patch tool); README-linux for the new flow
Tested with a temporary HOME: both unpack paths (msiextract: DLL, firmware, 96 patch files; Wine: + manuals), the
plug-in's lookup finds the files through access-dir.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
